# Line endings for the GENERATED runtime bundle and the fragments it is built
# from. Nothing else — see the note at the bottom before widening this.
#
# The problem this fixes, measured 2026-08-21:
#
#   src/shared/js/runtime/runtime.bundle.js is a concatenation of the fragments
#   beside it (tools/build-unit-runtime-bundle.js, `parts.join('\n')`). The
#   fragments were on disk as CRLF while their committed blobs were LF, so every
#   rebuild produced a CRLF bundle and `git diff` reported 16,158 insertions and
#   16,158 deletions with ZERO content change — CRLF-normalised, the rebuilt file
#   was byte-identical to HEAD.
#
#   Git never reported the fragments themselves, which is why this survived: the
#   index held each CRLF file's stat (speak.js: size 87,188) against its LF blob
#   (84,547), so a refresh compared stat, matched, and never re-hashed. They read
#   as clean while differing from HEAD at byte 3 of line 1. That is the signature
#   of a checkout made while core.autocrlf was true — which is still the value in
#   C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig; .git/config later set false, and a local
#   setting cannot undo a working tree that was already written.
#
#   It matters because CLAUDE.md requires a changed fragment and the regenerated
#   bundle to be committed together, and a one-line fragment change is invisible
#   inside a 16,158-line line-ending diff.
src/shared/js/runtime/*.js text eol=lf

# NOT widened to `* text=auto eol=lf` on purpose. 2,455 files are committed with
# CRLF today — 868 .json, 620 .php (src/moodle included), 303 .js, 278 .html,
# 46 .py, 43 .css — and a repo-wide rule marks every one of them for
# renormalisation at once. That is a legitimate change to make, but it is a
# deliberate one-commit sweep on a quiet tree, not something to inherit from a
# fix to the runtime bundle. Widen it when somebody is in a position to review
# 2,455 files, and re-run npm run check:php afterwards.
